{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For</b> — And the wicked shall perish in the days of evil and famine." "<b>Like the preciousness of rams</b> — Like the fat of sheep, as: 'with the fat of rams placed in smoke' — they vanish moment after moment." "And some say: <b>like the preciousness of rams</b> — like the grass of the valleys, like a broad כר, and similarly: ככר הירדן. And it is doubled, like: בבת עינו." "And the meaning of <b>in smoke</b> — as when the one who kindles a fire kindles it in them. The first כלו refers to the preciousness. And the second כלו refers to the wicked, and the word is proclitic on account of the end of the verse."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:58.818770937Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}